  "statement": "The numeral \\(47\\) in base \\(a\\) represents the same number as \\(74\\) in base \\(b.\\) Assuming both bases are positive integers, the least possible value of \\(a+b,\\) written as a Roman numeral, is:",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\mathrm{XIII}\\)"
    },
