  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1971-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The equality is \\(4a+7=7b+4,\\) or \\(4a-7b=-3.\\) Since both digits must be valid, \\(a,b\\gt7.\\) Reducing modulo \\(7\\) gives \\(a\\equiv1\\pmod7.\\) The first valid value is \\(a=15,\\) which gives \\(b=9.\\) Thus \\(a+b=24,\\) written \\(\\mathrm{XXIV}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Translate the numerals into \\(4a+7=7b+4\\)",
        "Both bases exceed \\(7\\); solve \\(4a-7b=-3\\) for the least valid pair"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
